  "place": "<div class=\"pg-facts\"><dl class=\"pg-rows\"><dt>Level</dt><dd>Denominación de Origen Calificada<span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://github.com/DjoeriT/Atlaslope/blob/main/data/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: MAPA, list of protected wine names\">MAPA list</a></span></span></dd></dl></div>",
  "weather": "<div class=\"pg-facts\"><div class=\"pg-fact\"><h4 class=\"pg-h3\">Measured climate</h4><div class=\"pg-chart pg-climate\"><dl class=\"pg-compare\"><div class=\"own\" style=\"--row: 0;\"><dt>Rioja</dt><dd><svg class=\"pg-stack\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 4\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Measured climate: Mild Mediterranean 40%, Oceanic 32%, Humid subtropical 24%, Other 4%\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"39.6\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#D2D45A\" data-i=\"0\" style=\"--seg: 0;\"><title>Mild Mediterranean 40%</title></rect><rect x=\"40\" y=\"0\" width=\"31.6\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#1F5F85\" data-i=\"1\" style=\"--seg: 1;\"><title>Oceanic 32%</title></rect><rect x=\"72\" y=\"0\" width=\"23.6\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#4FAE86\" data-i=\"2\" style=\"--seg: 2;\"><title>Humid subtropical 24%</title></rect><rect x=\"96\" y=\"0\" width=\"3.6000000000000036\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#D9D3C7\" data-i=\"3\" style=\"--seg: 3;\"><title>Other 4%</title></rect></svg></dd></div><div style=\"--row: 1;\"><dt>All of Spain</dt><dd><svg class=\"pg-stack\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 4\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Measured climate: All of Spain: Mild Mediterranean 21%, Oceanic 12%, Humid subtropical 6%, Other 61%\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"20.6\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#D2D45A\" data-i=\"0\" style=\"--seg: 0;\"><title>All of Spain: Mild Mediterranean 21%</title></rect><rect x=\"21\" y=\"0\" width=\"11.6\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#1F5F85\" data-i=\"1\" style=\"--seg: 1;\"><title>All of Spain: Oceanic 12%</title></rect><rect x=\"33\" y=\"0\" width=\"5.6\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#4FAE86\" data-i=\"2\" style=\"--seg: 2;\"><title>All of Spain: Humid subtropical 6%</title></rect><rect x=\"39\" y=\"0\" width=\"60.6\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#D9D3C7\" data-i=\"3\" style=\"--seg: 3;\"><title>All of Spain: Other 61%</title></rect></svg></dd></div></dl><ul class=\"pg-legend\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><li data-i=\"0\"><i style=\"background: rgb(210, 212, 90);\"></i>Mild Mediterranean 40%</li><li data-i=\"1\"><i style=\"background: rgb(31, 95, 133);\"></i>Oceanic 32%</li><li data-i=\"2\"><i style=\"background: rgb(79, 174, 134);\"></i>Humid subtropical 24%</li><li data-i=\"3\"><i style=\"background: rgb(217, 211, 199);\"></i>Other 4%</li></ul></div><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/21789074\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Köppen-Geiger: Beck et al. 2023, CC BY 4.0, 1991–2020\">Köppen-Geiger</a></span></span><p class=\"pg-note\">Measured the same way for each: the land inside the boundary.</p></div></div>",
  "ground": "<div class=\"pg-facts\"><div class=\"pg-fact\"><h4 class=\"pg-h3\">Altitude</h4><div class=\"pg-chart pg-altitude\"><dl class=\"pg-compare\"><div class=\"own\" style=\"--row: 0;\"><dt>Rioja</dt><dd><div class=\"pg-range\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Most of the land between 360 and 890 m, median 550 m\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 4\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"100\" height=\"4\" class=\"track\"></rect><rect x=\"18\" y=\"0\" width=\"26.5\" height=\"4\" class=\"fill\" style=\"transform-origin: 27.5% 50%;\"></rect><line x1=\"27.500000000000004\" x2=\"27.500000000000004\" y1=\"-2\" y2=\"6\" class=\"tick\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"></line></svg><span class=\"mid\" style=\"left: 27.5%;\">median 550 m</span><span class=\"lo\" style=\"right: 82%;\">360 m</span><span class=\"hi\" style=\"left: 44.5%;\">890 m</span></div></dd></div><div style=\"--row: 1;\"><dt>All of Spain</dt><dd><div class=\"pg-range\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Most of the land between 180 and 1,190 m, median 680 m\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 4\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"100\" height=\"4\" class=\"track\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"0\" width=\"50.5\" height=\"4\" class=\"fill\" style=\"transform-origin: 34% 50%;\"></rect><line x1=\"34\" x2=\"34\" y1=\"-2\" y2=\"6\" class=\"tick\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"></line></svg><span class=\"mid\" style=\"left: 34%;\">median 680 m</span><span class=\"lo\" style=\"right: 91%;\">180 m</span><span class=\"hi\" style=\"left: 59.5%;\">1,190 m</span></div></dd></div></dl></div><p>Most of the land between 360 and 890 m</p><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://github.com/DjoeriT/Atlaslope/blob/main/data/SOURCES.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Measured inside the boundary (Atlaslope, from Mapzen Terrarium elevation)\">Measured</a></span></span></div></div>",
  "rules": "<div class=\"pg-facts\"><div class=\"pg-fact\"><h4 class=\"pg-h3\">Famous styles</h4><ul class=\"pg-styles\"><li><strong>Crianza</strong><span>Reds aged at least two years, a year of it in oak barrel.</span></li><li><strong>Reserva</strong><span>Reds aged 36 months in oak and bottle, at least 12 in barrel.</span></li><li><strong>Gran Reserva</strong><span>Reds aged 60 months in oak and bottle, at least 24 in barrel.</span></li></ul><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://riojawine.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/pliego-de-condiciones-de-la-doca-rioja-en-vigor.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Pliego de condiciones DOCa Rioja (Consejo Regulador copy, amendments to AM10)\">Pliego · pp. 10–11</a></span></span></div><div class=\"pg-fact\"><h4 class=\"pg-h3\">Main grapes</h4><ul class=\"pg-grapes\"><li>Tempranillo</li><li>Viura (Macabeo)</li></ul><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://es.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=174986857\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Wikipedia (es), «Rioja (vino)», revision 174986857\">Wikipedia</a></span></span></div><dl class=\"pg-rows\"><dt>Also allowed</dt><dd>Alarije, Subirat Parent, Malvasía Riojana, Turruntés, Verdejo, Tempranillo Blanco, Sauvignon Blanco, Mazuela, Maturana Tinta, Maturana Blanca, Graciano, Garnacha Tinta, Garnacha Blanca, Chardonnay <button type=\"button\" class=\"more\" aria-expanded=\"true\">Show fewer</button><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/eambrosia-api/api/v1/attachments/30985\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Documento único PDO-ES-A0117 (EU single document, Rioja)\">EU single document · p. 5</a></span></span></dd><dt>Wine types</dt><dd>Dry and semi-dry whites, rosados and reds, plus semi-sweet and sweet whites and rosados; reds sold young or aged.<span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/eambrosia-api/api/v1/attachments/30985\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Documento único PDO-ES-A0117 (EU single document, Rioja)\">EU single document · p. 1</a></span></span></dd></dl></div>"
 },
 "taste": "<section id=\"taste\" class=\"pg-answer\" aria-labelledby=\"taste-h\"><h2 id=\"taste-h\" tabindex=\"-1\">How it tastes</h2><div class=\"pg-cards\"><div class=\"red\"><b><i class=\"pg-sw red\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>Reds</b><p>purple when young, cherry-garnet as crianza, ruby-brick as gran reserva; intense fruit, toasted oak, then spice with age.</p></div><div class=\"white\"><b><i class=\"pg-sw white\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>Whites</b><p>pale straw with lemon-green rims; green fruit, flowers.</p></div><div class=\"rose\"><b><i class=\"pg-sw rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>Rosés</b><p>strawberry; red fruit, floral notes.</p></div></div><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/eambrosia-api/api/v1/attachments/30985\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Documento único PDO-ES-A0117 (EU single document, Rioja)\">EU single document · p. 1</a></span></span></section>",
 "short": "<section id=\"short\" class=\"pg-short\" aria-labelledby=\"short-h\"><h2 id=\"short-h\" tabindex=\"-1\">In short</h2><ol><li><span class=\"k\">Grapes</span><span class=\"f\"><a href=\"#place=rioja&amp;page\">Tempranillo and Viura (Macabeo)</a><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://es.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=174986857\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Wikipedia (es), «Rioja (vino)», revision 174986857\">Wikipedia</a></span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"k\">Climate</span><span class=\"f\"><a href=\"#place=rioja&amp;page\">Atlantic and Mediterranean influences meet; temperatures are mild and annual rainfall is about 400 mm.</a><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/eambrosia-api/api/v1/attachments/30985\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Documento único PDO-ES-A0117 (EU single document, Rioja)\">EU single document · p. 5</a></span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"k\">Soil</span><span class=\"f\"><a href=\"#place=rioja&amp;page\">Clay-limestone (a quarter), ferrous clay (a quarter) and alluvial soils near the rivers (half).</a><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://riojawine.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/pliego-de-condiciones-de-la-doca-rioja-en-vigor.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Pliego de condiciones DOCa Rioja (Consejo Regulador copy, amendments to AM10)\">Pliego · p. 15</a></span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"k\">Zones</span><span class=\"f\"><a href=\"#place=rioja&amp;page\">3 zones, from Rioja Alta to Rioja Oriental.</a></span></li><li><span class=\"k\">Style</span><span class=\"f\"><a href=\"#place=rioja&amp;page\">Crianza. Reds aged at least two years, a year of it in oak barrel.</a><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://riojawine.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/pliego-de-condiciones-de-la-doca-rioja-en-vigor.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Pliego de condiciones DOCa Rioja (Consejo Regulador copy, amendments to AM10)\">Pliego · pp. 10–11</a></span></span></span></li></ol></section>",
 "producers": "<section id=\"producers\" aria-labelledby=\"producers-h\"><h2 id=\"producers-h\" tabindex=\"-1\">Producers</h2><ul class=\"pg-names\"><li>Marqués de Murrieta</li></ul><span class=\"src short\"><span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1368867539\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Source: Wikipedia (en), «Rioja DOCa», revision 1368867539\">Wikipedia</a></span></span></section>"
